-tailed** critical region for the test statistic is approximately $T \\le$\n{{field-2}}.\n\nAt the $1%$ level of significance, there is\n{{field-3}}\nevidence that the sleep app improved sleep quality.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Hypothesis Tests for Means of Paired-Samples: Applications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050920 :topic/math-academy-id 4944 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for Two Means: Paired-Sample T-Test"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204443 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202599}] :question/math-academy-id "q-251486" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $8$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_{2}, …, x_{8}$, and $y_{1}, y_{2}, …, y_{8}$.\n\nYou are given that\n$∑_(i = 1)^(8)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2} = 1.6,; ∑_(i = 1)^(8)(y_{i} - y^(―))^{2} = 5.1,; ∑_(i = 1)^(8)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)) = 2.3$.\n\nThen, $S_{xy} =$\n{{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202601} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202602} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202603} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202604} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202605}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202600}] :question/math-academy-id "q-251488" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$x_{i}$** | $5$ | $11$ | $9$ | $12$ | $18